# Inkling-2-Mini-1x-DGX-Spark configuration. Copy to .env (git-ignored). Precedence: environment > .env > profile > defaults.
# Commands that need no node (help, print-serve, build's refusals, the tests) run with NODES empty.
NODES=                             # ONE management address or host name of the node (ssh user SSH_USER, key-based); empty: no node
SSH_USER=spark
# NODE_NAME=node-3                 # scripts/final_run.sh only: the name (node-1..node-4) the records carry; the address above never enters a tracked file
BASE_DIR=/home/spark/inkling-2-mini-1x-dgx-spark   # on the node: bin/ (engine), src/, target/, logs/ (serve.log, memguard.*), run/ (pids, node.lock)
SMALL_MODEL_DIR=/home/spark/models/Inkling-2-Small-EXL3-4bpw   # the Small's pack on the node: engine-test goldens (the Small's drafter hash test) reads its mtp.safetensors, read-only
MODELS_DIR=/home/spark/models      # the pack lands in MODELS_DIR/Inkling-2-Mini-SAGE-REXL3-4.23bpw (config/pins.sh MODEL_NAME)
HF_BIN=/home/spark/venvs/hf/bin/hf # the hf CLI on the node (setup installs a venv there when it is missing)
CACHE_DIR=/home/spark/.cache/inkling-2-mini-1x-dgx-spark   # HF_HOME of the download
CONTAINER=inkling-2-mini-1x-dgx-spark   # the engine runs as a native process; the name is only allowed to appear in `docker ps` beside it
SERVED_NAME=inkling-2-mini-1x-dgx-spark
PORT=8000                          # the HTTP API (--host 0.0.0.0 --port PORT)
API_KEY=                           # the engine has no API key: the controller REFUSES a non-empty value (as CYBERFROST does);
                                   # keep the port on a private network
# REXL3_SRC=$HOME/projects/rexl3-inkling2-loop   # local engine git repository `build` stages from (the default; give a full path to change it)
PROFILE=bootstrap                  # config/profiles/PROFILE.env: bootstrap (262,144 x 4), long (1,048,576 x 2), max (1,048,576 x 4);
                                   # all PROFILE_MEASURED=0 until a record says otherwise (docs/FIT.md)

# ── serving (./inkling2mini.sh print-serve shows the resulting command line) ──────────────────────────────────────
MAX_MODEL_LEN=                     # --max-model-len; empty: the profile's
SLOTS=                             # --slots (concurrent sequences); empty: the profile's
KV_TOKENS=                         # --kv-tokens: the int8 KV pool in tokens; empty: SLOTS x MAX_MODEL_LEN (every lane full)
PREFILL_CHUNK=4096                 # --prefill-chunk
# The drafter (4.6), the prefix cache (4.5) and the vision tower (4.7) exist and work together: the drafter serves image prompts (their rows
# are ordinary rows of the forward, their taps feed its context), its state rides in the cache's snapshots, and the cache keys an image by
# its content (a cut is never inside an image). These are the shipping defaults; each has its gate record (docs/DECISIONS.md).
SPEC=dspark                        # --spec: dspark (the pack's block drafter, the engine's learnt plan budget: wins on code, tool calls,
                                   # JSON and reasoning, about break-even to -10 % on prose: docs/DECISIONS.md), none (serial), copy (copy
                                   # drafter) or auto (dspark with the copy drafter for streams it cannot serve; untested)
PREFIX_CACHE=on                    # on: --prefix-cache on (the engine refuses the boot when the plan leaves no room for two entries);
                                   # off: --prefix-cache off; auto: no flag (on only when the KV plan leaves memory spare); a whole
                                   # number: --prefix-cache-mib N (0 disables). Text and image prompts alike; the tower's bytes come first
VISION=on                          # off: --no-vision; on: load the vision tower and serve image parts (with or without the cache and the drafter)
MEMORY_FLOOR_GIB=                  # the engine's MemAvailable floor at boot, GiB >= 0.25: REXL3_MEMORY_FLOOR_GIB; empty: the engine default 8
EXTRA_FLAGS=                       # more rexl3-serve flags, appended last (e.g. "--kv-tokens 4194304")
EXTRA_ENV=                         # more KEY=VALUE words in the server's environment (no spaces inside a value)
# Bring-up only, NEVER a default: the one way past the engine's component gate for a component that is required and not built
# (none is missing since the forward passed its oracle comparison). Every record made with it says so.
# EXTRA_ENV=REXL3_ALLOW_UNGATED_COMPONENTS=1
PROFILE_LANES=                      # bench profile: concurrent window-length prompts after the solo one; empty: SLOTS, 1: none
PROFILE_SOLO=1                      # bench profile: 0 skips the solo window-length prompt (the lanes run still samples memory)
PROFILE_SAMPLE_S=5                  # bench profile: seconds between the node-side samples of GPU MiB and MemAvailable
NEEDLE_MAX_TOKENS=1024              # bench needle: new tokens per request; the pack reasons first, 128 ends the reply inside the reasoning
READY_TIMEOUT_S=1800               # start: wait this long for /health (200)
STOP_GRACE_S=60                    # stop: SIGTERM, then SIGKILL after this many seconds
BUILD_TIMEOUT_S=3600               # build: cargo is killed after this many seconds
# MemAvailable the node needs before doctor/start/fetch. docs/FIT.md: MemTotal 121.69 GiB minus ~11 GiB for the OS, the CUDA
# context and the unaccounted leaves ~110 GiB on an idle node (engine budget ~100.7 plus the ~10 GiB floor); one Inkling-2-Small
# rank holds ~73 GiB, so a node that still carries a rank or another stack reads far below. 100 separates the two, as the Small's
# recipe does. The Mini loads 14 GiB, so this is a gate for an idle node, not the engine's need: the `bootstrap` profile needs
# about 14.00 + 5 + 0.63 + 8.6 (prefix cache, the window rule at 4 x 262,144: docs/FIT.md) + 18.14 (KV) GiB plus the engine floor; the `max` profile's KV (72.56 GiB) is what
# makes the idle-node figure matter (docs/FIT.md).
MIN_AVAIL_GIB=100
# The GPU SM clock cap is not a setting: 2,200 MHz, pinned in config/pins.sh (GPU_CLOCK_CAP_MHZ). It is hardware protection, applied
# (sudo -n nvidia-smi -lgc) before every `start` and every GPU test with its success line required, and never released, raised or
# changed. The old GPU_CLOCKS key must be absent or equal to the pin.

# ── memory guard (scripts/memguard.sh, mandatory: start fails and kills the server unless the guard armed on its pid) ──
# SIGKILLs the server when MemAvailable stays under the floor for 3 samples (0.5 s apart) or swap grows past the cap, and
# records the MemAvailable minimum (BASE_DIR/logs/memguard.min; ./inkling2mini.sh memwatch begin|report).
GUARD_START_MIB=2048               # floor while the pack loads
GUARD_MIB=1024                     # floor once /health answers 200
GUARD_SWAP_MAX_MIB=64              # swap growth since the guard armed that kills the server...
GUARD_SWAP_AVAIL_MIB=8192          # ...counted only while MemAvailable is under this: the engine's 8 GiB floor
DROP_CACHES_EVERY_S=20             # page-cache drop while loading (sudo -n; 0 = never); GB10 counts only free memory

ALLOWED_CONTAINERS="other-service-1 other-service-2"   # containers that may run on the node beside the server (doctor fails on any other)

# The Inkling-2-Small TP4 group (container-free rexl3-serve ranks on all four Sparks) normally owns the GPU. These run on THIS
# machine, only when someone types `stop-other` / `restore-other`; no other command, test or doctor calls them. Stopping any one
# rank ends the whole group. `restore-other` stops this server first, then runs RESTORE_OTHER. The Small's `start` does not apply
# the GPU clock cap and the lock does not survive a reboot or a driver reload, so RESTORE_OTHER first locks every rank at the cap
# with the Small controller's own `gpu-clocks MHZ` (the number is GPU_CLOCK_CAP_MHZ of config/pins.sh; a test checks they agree)
# and starts only if every rank took it: the cap is hardware protection, in place whenever any work runs on any node.
STOP_OTHER="cd ~/recipes/Inkling-2-Small-EXL3-4bpw-4x-DGX-Spark && ./inkling2.sh stop"
RESTORE_OTHER="cd ~/recipes/Inkling-2-Small-EXL3-4bpw-4x-DGX-Spark && ./inkling2.sh gpu-clocks 2200 && ./inkling2.sh start"
